{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QouSu2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QouSu2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2_adjoint_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2_adjoint_dim","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The adjoint of SU(2) has dimension 3 (spin-1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2Observable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2Observable","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L48-L60","doc":"SU(2) satisfies all observability conditions. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:qou-su2","label":"ex:qou-su2","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.volume_form_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.volume_form_exists","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L46-L46","doc":"(iii) The fundamental V = ℂ² admits a non-degenerate alternating form\nε : Λ²V → ℂ, forcing det(g_V) = 1 for all gauge transformations.\nWitnessed by: Λ²ℂ² ≅ ℂ, i.e. exteriorPowerDim = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.exteriorPowerDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.exteriorPowerDim","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Dimension of the exterior power Λ²V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.adj_dim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.adj_dim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The dimension of the adjoint is 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.adjoint_irreducible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.adjoint_irreducible","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Schur lemma: adjoint_dim ≠ 1 means no trivial summand,\nhence irreducible in the SU(2) case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.adjoint_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.adjoint_dim","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L35-L35","doc":"(ii) The adjoint representation Ad ≅ V₁ (spin-1, dim 3) is\nirreducible with no invariant vectors: Hom(𝟙, V₁) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.haar_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.haar_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L32-L32","doc":"(i) The Haar integral is faithful (non-degenerate Frobenius form).\nWitnessed by: fundamental dim > 0 ensures non-trivial pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.fundamentalDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.fundamentalDim","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Dimension of the fundamental representation V = ℂ². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2ObservabilityData","kind":"structure","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-su2.lean#L22-L46","doc":"**SU(2) observability data**: the three conditions that make\nRep(SU(2)) a quantum observable universe.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:qou-su2}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}